Governmental claims-maximum liability 25LSO-0130, 1.1
amounts.
FISCAL NOTE
This bill increases the maximum liability amounts for claims authorized under the
Wyoming Governmental Claims Act.
The Department of Administration and Information (Department) states that the
increased maximum claim amounts in the bill will result in increased expenditures
from the State Self Insurance Pool (Pool) for increased claims.
The Department currently estimates an increase in claims expenditures ranging
from $681,553 to $894,539 per year (an increase ranging from 8 to 10.5 percent).
The Department used two other government liability pool estimates to arrive at
this fiscal impact range, based on current claims and projections utilizing
historical data. This estimate does not include the potential increase in the
number of claims resulting from the increased claim maximums, therefore this
range may be underestimated. The Department is in the process of obtaining an
actuarial study to refine this fiscal impact estimate.
The increase in the claim maximums will require additional funding for the State
Self Insurance Pool for increased claims. The Department’s request for this
additional funding is included in the Agency Estimate of Administrative Impact
referenced below.
NOTICE-AGENCY ESTIMATE OF ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT REQUESTED
This bill has administrative impact that appears to increase duties or
responsibilities of one or more state agencies and may impact agency spending or
staffing requirements. As introduced, the bill does not modify any state agency
budget or current personnel authorizations.
The following state agencies will be asked to provide their estimate of the
administrative fiscal impact prior to the first committee meeting held to
consider the bill:
Dept. of Administration & Information
